  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to scatter, to make a mess, to clutter",
      "explanation": "To cause disorder by spreading things around untidily."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "04360_chirakasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{部屋|へや}を{散|ち}らかすな。",
      "english": "Don't make a mess of the room.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04360_chirakasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}がおもちゃを{散|ち}らかした。",
      "english": "The child made a mess with toys.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04360_chirakasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{片付|かたづ}けたばかりなのに、また{散|ち}らかさないでください。",
      "english": "I just cleaned up, so please don't make a mess again.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Intransitive pair: {散|ち}らかる (to be messy).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates resulting state or ongoing action. {散|ち}らかしている = 'has made messy' or 'is making messy.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xを{散|ち}らかす (to scatter X, make X messy)\n- {部屋|へや}を{散|ち}らかす (to mess up a room)\n- {散|ち}らかさないで (don't make a mess)\n\nINTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {散|ち}らかす (transitive) - to make messy\n- {散|ち}らかる (intransitive) - to be messy\n\nNOTE: Often used in negative requests: {散|ち}らかさないで！ (Don't make a mess!)",
